oid generating a warning if it is not available since some builds do not have it.  BUG=b:24569990 TEST=cbuildbot_unittest  Change-Id: Icc9275ed5ecd1f8af96be553d59745a08ca8179c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330920 Commit-Ready: David Riley &lt;davidriley@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Riley &lt;davidriley@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David James &lt;davidjames@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="330920" owner_email="davidriley@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/20/330920/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I10ede611e6c1714141c95821e9c3e8d6cc753d0f" commit="a2479fca6af77a763e1cddb775691f256be65386" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ALSA: hda - Allow unlimited pins and converters in patch_hdmi.c  Use the dynamic array allocations for pins, converters and PCM arrays instead of the fixed size arrays.  The modern HDMI codecs get more and more pins, and we don't know the sensitive limit.  Most of the patch are spent for the straight conversions from the fixed array access to snd_array helpers.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49317 TEST=verified audio output on both DP and HDMI  Change-Id: I10ede611e6c1714141c95821e9c3e8d6cc753d0f Signed-off-by: Takashi Iwai &lt;tiwai@suse.de&gt; Signed-off-by: ravikira &lt;ravi.k.yerraguntla@intel.com&gt; (cherry-pick from bce0d2a80e428aac3b39bf19675f1f57126f9cb6) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329388 Commit-Ready: Ravi Yerraguntla &lt;ravi.k.yerraguntla@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Ravi Yerraguntla &lt;ravi.k.yerraguntla@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="329388" owner_email="ravi.k.yerraguntla@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/88/329388/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I0331928fdbb4b3d49d27cc05f6a0f5e8285e49e8" commit="65361f06a48b2a29cfe07480b4ae42fac67c0897" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ALSA: hda - Avoid choose same converter for unused pins  For Intel Haswell HDMI codecs, the pins choose converter 0 by default. This would cause conflict when playing audio on unused pins,the pin with physical device connected would get audio data too. i.e. Pin 0/1/2 default choose converter 0, pin 1 has HDMI monitor connected. when play audio on Pin 0 or pin 2, pin 1 could get audio data too.  This patch configure unused pins to choose different converter.  Signed-off-by: Wang Xingchao &lt;xingchao.wang@linux.intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Takashi Iwai &lt;tiwai@suse.de&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49317 TEST=verified audio output on both DP and HDMI  Change-Id: I0331928fdbb4b3d49d27cc05f6a0f5e8285e49e8 Signed-off-by: ravikira &lt;ravi.k.yerraguntla@intel.com&gt; (cherry-pick from 7ef166b831237e67b2ea83ce0c933c46ddd6eb26) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329389 Commit-Ready: Ravi Yerraguntla &lt;ravi.k.yerraguntla@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Ravi Yerraguntla &lt;ravi.k.yerraguntla@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="329389" owner_email="ravi.k.yerraguntla@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/89/329389/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1c0984ddb4e9cb0a2d39a29fa1d2522adde866b6" commit="2554aaf0ae94cdf5d24d4384ac3b3e1448d0aef7" commit_message="purge_lib_unittest: Simplify GS mocking.  Reorganize the tests a little to reduce duplication.  BUG=None TEST=Ran tests.  Change-Id: I1c0984ddb4e9cb0a2d39a29fa1d2522adde866b6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330421 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="330421" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/21/330421/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie57ee0352b25ec6df9f45ea0c92e2358001692ad" commit="565a3a2ca9e93df3cb2912f860a7f55cb6cd5e00" commit_message="purge_builds: Parallelize candidate expiration.  BUG=None TEST=Manual + lint + unittets  Change-Id: Ie57ee0352b25ec6df9f45ea0c92e2358001692ad Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330422 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="330422" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/22/330422/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I73a840ae321820212e50d609dab17576117a7d64" commit="953e98fd075e49eec8a657b9f55bb85d9f6f4223" commit_message="npcx: Add 1.8V IO support for some GPIOs and I2C pins.  Add 1.8V IO support for some GPIOs and I2C pins. We use a array (gpio_lvol_table) to confine which IO pins can switch to 1.8V. Before setting it to support low voltage level, FW should set IO pin's type to open-drain and disable internal pulling up or down.  We also add examples in gpio.inc of npcx_evb and npcx_evb_arm to indicate how to set GPIO &amp; I2C pins to 1.8V if user adds CONFIG_TEST_1P8V definition in board.h.  In i2c.c driver, this version removes the internal pull-up feature of i2c ports since the driving force is too weak. (about 30K ohm)  Modified sources: 1. gpio.c: Add 1.8V IO support for some GPIOs and I2C pins. 2. i2c.c: Remove internal pull-ups feature for i2c pins and move 1.8V    support to gpio.c. 3. register.h: Modified NPCX_LV_GPIO_CTL register &amp; bits definitions. 4. npcx_evb\gpio.inc: Add examples of 1.8V IO. 5. npcx_evb_arm\gpio.inc: Add examples of 1.8V IO.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:34346 TEST=make buildall -j; test nuvoton IC specific drivers BRANCH=none  Change-Id: I73a840ae321820212e50d609dab17576117a7d64 Signed-off-by: Mulin Chao &lt;mlchao@nuvoton.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330037 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="330037" owner_email="mlchao@nuvoton.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/37/330037/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I348662d63c4a2d730ad4f2941cd4cdd3c631125e" commit="f323fca150e6864048f812cc093b7001ab30b41b" commit_message="autotest(wifi): Allow shill_proxy to set optional manager property  Manager DHCPProperty.Hostname and DHCPProperty.VendorClass are optional properties.  If they have been previously set from the command line or other dbus call, the network_WiFi_SetOptionalDhcpProperties test is successful.  If they have not been set, they will not be returned in the GetProperties call for the Manager, this causes the test to fail.  This CL adds an optional call to set the properties if they were not included in the GetProperties list.  Also includes one docstring fix to pass presubmit check.  BUG=chromium:589595 TEST=deleted optional property settings with: \ stop shill; rm /var/cache/shill/default/profile; start shill TEST=verified the properties were not set with: \ dbus-send --system --print-reply --dest=org.chromium.flimflam / \ org.chromium.flimflam.Manager.GetProperties TEST=test_that -b daisy chromeos2-row6-rack4-host2.cros \ network_WiFi_SetOptionalDhcpProperties  Change-Id: I348662d63c4a2d730ad4f2941cd4cdd3c631125e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330414 Commit-Ready: Rebecca Silberstein &lt;silberst@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Rebecca Silberstein &lt;silberst@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: mukesh agrawal &lt;quiche@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="330414" owner_email="silberst@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/14/330414/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1abf64994fe1060464ade1a30f4953e09028ada6" commit="4a025096eb305dd946c484b99ea74640a70e9439" commit_message="chrome: Assert find_dependencies result in the subshell environment  assert checks the value of $PIPESTATUS (*), but command substitution is invoked in a subshell environement (**) so the assert in the existing code results in no-op.  *: https://devmanual.gentoo.org/ebuild-writing/error-handling/index.html **: https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/Command-Execution-Environment.html  BUG=chromium:590762 TEST=rm ~/chrome/src/tools/perf/find_dependencies and emerge-${BOARD} chromeos-chrome to see it actually fails  Change-Id: I1abf64994fe1060464ade1a30f4953e09028ada6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330226 Commit-Ready: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="330226" owner_email="hashimoto@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/26/330226/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch=